# Mutation cases for §scxml-6.4 — what cancelling an invocation may discard.
#
# Run with `scripts/mutate sce-build/tests/mutations/done_invoke_outlives_the_invoking_state.cases`.
#
# Cancelling stops a session that is still running, and what that session
# sends from then on is not the parent's to process (W3C SCXML Test 252). A
# session that already ended — it entered a top-level <final>, ran its exit
# handlers and sent done.invoke — has nothing left to stop, and what it sent
# before it ended is still the parent's: Test 236 leaves the invoking state on
# the event the child's exit handler sent, and takes done.invoke after it.
#
# Measured 2026-09-24 on the Interpreter's move onto Appendix D's main event
# loop: Test 236 failed on the C++ W3C suite, the pybind11 suite and the ctest
# W3C target at once. The cancel had always purged the parent's queue of the
# session's events and filtered the rest. What kept that from reaching
# done.invoke was the delivery it replaced, as its code reads: the raiser took
# the whole queue into a local list before dispatching any of it, so the purge
# found nothing left to remove, and handed each event over without its origin
# session, so the filter could not recognise it.
#
# The Test 252 half — a running session's later events stay discarded — has no
# case here. Its witness is W3C SCXML Test 252 itself, which the W3C suites run
# on every channel; no integration test holds it, and this harness reaches the
# W3C suites only through a ctest target that runs all 404 cases.
#
# Anchors are literal slices of the source; an edit that moves one is reported
# INCONCLUSIVE with the anchor quoted, never as a pass.

mutation_ctest --test-dir build -R '^IntegrationTests$'
mutation_targets sce/src/runtime/InvokeExecutor.cpp
mutation_oracles tests/integration/DoneInvokeOutlivesTheInvokingStateTest.cpp

# ── C++ Interpreter: a session that ended is cancelled as if running ──
#
# The defect as it shipped: the cancel does not ask whether the session is
# still running, so a child that ended before its invoking state was left
# loses the done.invoke it sent last.

mutation_case "a cancel discards what a session that already ended sent" <<'PY'
edit("sce/src/runtime/InvokeExecutor.cpp",
     """    const bool stillRunning = child != nullptr && child->isRunning();""",
     """    const bool stillRunning = child != nullptr;""")
PY
